# Gate EVERY HTTP request to this stack behind HTTP Basic auth — /setup,
# /status, /packages, /call, /unsigned, /facts, /logs, /destroy. Each one runs a
# command on a computer, and /setup enrolls a key that may administer the
# chassis inside it. (Health checks on /healthz stay open.)
#
# The password is a TENANT SECRET. Set it, and the gate opens to whoever has it:
#   txco auth tenant secrets set EXAMPLE_NODE_PW --tenant <this stack's tenant>
# then reach the stack as user `human`, password = that secret.
#
# secrets.password.optional=true lets the op RUN when the secret is unset (so it
# can emit a verdict and a 401 rather than being skipped);
# allow_unconfigured=false is the DECISION, visible here: this stack FAILS
# CLOSED — no EXAMPLE_NODE_PW set ⇒ 401 everywhere. The secret never reaches the
# envelope: the op consumes it and emits only a verdict
# (@computed.basic_auth_ok), compared constant-time.
WHEN @src == "http" && @web.req.url.path != "/healthz"
  WITH user = "human",
       secrets.password.secret = "EXAMPLE_NODE_PW",
       secrets.password.optional = true,
       allow_unconfigured = false
  EXEC "txco://basic-auth-verify"
